      "path": "src/modules/reference-catalog/catalog.ts",
      "content": "Handle these new failure outcomes in the workspace initialization path as well. In `src/coordinators/workspace/workspace.ts:239–249`, every non-Seeded catalog result is converted to an empty additions list and initialization still returns `Opened`. Consequently, exhausting these retries can open a workspace whose required defaults are still missing, and RuntimeNotWritable is swallowed using the earlier readiness result. Propagate the refusal or return a retryable initialization failure before reporting Opened.",
      "existing_code": "  | { readonly kind: 'Conflict' }\n  | { readonly kind: 'RuntimeNotWritable' };",
      "start_line": 32,
      "end_line": 33,
      "category": "bug",
      "severity": "medium"
    },
    {
      "path": "src/modules/reference-catalog/catalog.ts",
      "content": "Use the imported `RuntimeNotWritable` type instead of a kind-only replacement. Persistence returns recovery details (`runtimeReadiness`, `failedChecks`, `workspaceStatus`, and `safeActions`), but this public return type erases them, so a caller narrowing a seed result to RuntimeNotWritable cannot access the recovery information or forward it to an API expecting the shared refusal type. This also differs from CatalogSaveResult in this file.",
      "suggestion_code": "  | RuntimeNotWritable;",
      "existing_code": "  | { readonly kind: 'RuntimeNotWritable' };",
